      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4385768077",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Relation prediction for knowledge graphs aims at predicting missing relationships between entities.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:04ef10190e2d5a7123b621b80947431cc3d4ad4e16f01d8cbd2620c7419d23e8",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "69b25cadb6be5c732e34e8ea7ba3e9bb5919eef55cdd6e37688505edaeff4ab5",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:24:36.715775Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:88265f161e1f43d2afa9581172372a93ad688ce5e8ff2b128ecef3cae824faa6#results[11];abstract[0:99]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W3113170987",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Recently, various methods based on Graph Neural Networks (GNN) have been proposed for the problem and achieved impressive prediction performance.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:0831b3cebdf698d9f249dd41ec622fa6ff04cc6ad5d76f2980bc90d8e9d21cee",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "6c4c1df3332c85cf964ecb3ba7313e85cfde6be47fd9f7d6619fa2e581d97f68",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:27:41.911376Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:48e9d1f6be7c4b12a367e6ce93642bbf9ac2105003585e8013ad636b048505f3#results[2];abstract[111:256]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4393159807",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Graph unlearning, which aims to eliminate the influence of specific nodes, edges, or attributes from a trained Graph Neural Network (GNN), is essential in applications where privacy, bias, or data obsolescence is a concern.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:0b1ba38a5f7fa695de7d6309571afe200ff34a0b3d7a4c2f5178e592d3f858d9",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "d64c2b66abb0851026ae31efa15336ceb6b19691c4d440ba19c88a0cba0a2cdb",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:29:04.205472Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:fc3f64666ea8847d206a32dac019053cfa21f47fb3fd5714776f5d60004fa4f9#results[18];abstract[0:223]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4409364817",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "As instances that appear in the real world are naturally connected and can be represented with graphs, graph neural networks become increasingly popular in tackling the anomaly detection problem.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:12bd22be1beb2d14b0bf9ac38a08f5df0f2a7d7d3fe18e4834bc4662ad0bc9e5",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "7a2e64ae41a687242a99fc98b29089a552aa73e206bf44b0e7c5d3a1ba19ae92",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:30:23.328057Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:8fbadd4d5611e2cde37692d567262013f0af08c2a4767f5d96cfa2bada53bf69#results[0];abstract[118:313]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4385768068",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Federated graph learning is a widely recognized technique that promotes collaborative training of graph neural networks (GNNs) by multi-client graphs.However, existing approaches heavily rely on the communication of model parameters or gradients for federated optimization and fail to adequately address the data heterogeneity introduced by intricate and diverse graph distributions.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:132efaf606bbde7188c33eefd8fae99cec3f9a1cfe465a96258e6b069eba8317",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "fbccb6e9eb4aa2c980682e23ddab20e5ffcec71aeb2d748adea413e025dd8750",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:31:16.843757Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:d8f2ed8af477efc6f15356cb58e88b0b7280383958fea81aa8896689a7e974b2#results[9];abstract[0:383]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4414359577",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "With these considerations, PASSAT numerically solves the advection equation and the Navier-Stokes equation on the spherical manifold, utilizes a spherical graph neural network to capture the Earth-atmosphere interaction, and generates the initial velocity fields that are critical to solving the advection equation from the same spherical graph neural network.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:167377c5f51fca3d5edfd88f5a7db82f71a28c52b424184723f031eb07200c71",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "b47e3495ccc083c8c2e20676bc8795587e46bbdb9342898c3d438c21d6ea1306",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:31:19.002717Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:37e8ee9ac0bed54aa6217aa646f183f4110401422870823e708444f8cf16dd84#results[17];abstract[723:1083]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4414360247",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Graph Convolutional Networks (GCNs) achieve an impressive performance due to the remarkable representation ability in learning the graph information.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:176857df730f0835de94ce48dd3a8406787e44e6b013319eff1c92c4bc116502",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "4bc1494aecd03e3bc99a8aedff861a84bed347afdc00983b8cc46b1e4f5cf179",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:30:09.168460Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:43787e74995b3cb837ea01a73e40b900d0ad0d8c218fe73989f5709a66f3f134#results[10];abstract[0:149]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4285606073",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "We develop a series of algorithms, including graph construction, learning, and pre-training.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:1857cd178f95588e7c53c97c5e02f709317dc92a83eb69e220df7a1329c84376",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "caafdf1a51d6aa626c26a89c77520de0d4ea26b81c9c051064d8c12a5f103456",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:27:12.673536Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:c0ba5929b5e63c25005eb60f38d03c7b21d156742b3613546f2ccd82bfcc2a1d#results[40];abstract[903:995]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4382202654",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "To address these issues, we propose Target-oriented Graph Neural Network (TGNN), a novel framework that goes beyond traditional consistency by prioritizing task-relevant information, ensuring alignment with the target.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:21b8b42a536e52d859d738b4d027dedb1d86fa7f61db30a88408d1cecc10b0fd",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "cc9aeb5222573b8aff150b5e360d859f88818f0aa2c1e9a3cca70e3cacbde99d",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:31:12.240122Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:558ed5d0dd3f350614dd0e3ab202ba757f11232910382e9081bf6f35db95850f#results[11];abstract[603:821]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4414359912",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Extensive evaluations over real benchmark datasets show that our proposed method, namely Local Similarity Graph Neural Network (LSGNN), can offer comparable or superior state-of-the-art performance on both homophilic and heterophilic graphs.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:2526460662715ddbc490d6be1c9ed805a335b857ec7f4fff0d2190a29d591b45",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "89a27031ebc2c3a9592e075cacc03e4cc91d4dc3463e80279946b3b31512f7fe",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:30:28.832851Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:1c81f5a0a513ef77b4d5ddc6cd4535046603eabd5011132f051f56c2b29624d9#results[4];abstract[784:1025]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4385764100",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "To completely solve these problems, we first propose the priori anchor graph regularization (PAGG) for scalable multi-view bipartite graph clustering, dubbed as SMGC method.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:3ef28e661f2f7f4fd1288d2159313b73bf1ffe234896fe749121d4f2761a2549",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "a0139f7f1c06e4458afc1c7db4b3323126ad262771ef3e6c670790bad7b16b07",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:27:04.423443Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:5781a00914f12a82de36b8ef6c5c0eae60cd92498400f02c779ef7fc0395768f#results[20];abstract[466:639]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4382202986",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Diffusion-based molecular graph generative models have achieved significant success in template-free, single-step retrosynthesis prediction.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:40155e879d76a19175f888c241373af25f03a31dcb7892417f48ceba6757ab3f",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "dd02256a4c38e9b284608dad643f251dd59bd3a4a1a9ae0e7763fe6fb1dc6a05",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:29:22.052491Z",
